Z||000001||malacite||11-29-2001||10:58 AM||||my fiero died on my way home from  fiero meeting.<BR>all i had left was the wheels.<BR>i needed to sell these wheels so i could afford to make the down payment on another car. (no fieros for me for a while) anyway the wheel sale fell through four or five times.<BR>now i'm stuck with a set of wheels that won't fit anything and incredibly high monthly payments for a car that won't get out of it's own way.<P>that and i dropped a christmas tree on my head at work and had a sore neck for three days. the idiot customer i was getting it down for didn't even ask me if i was ok. she might have laughed a little but i'm not sure.<P>how's that? did i win?<P>------------------<BR>Malacite<P>Grendel-88 Fiero RIP<BR>'94 Saturn SW2 RallySport<BR>'95 Saturn SL1 Touring||||reg||9
Z||000002||Raydar||11-29-2001||11:23 AM||||I know of a bad day that <I>someone else</I> had...<P>I used to fix the radio system belonging to one of the metro Atlanta area police departments. <BR>On days that traffic court was in session, parking was completely absurd. You had to get there very early, or park like 1/4 - 1/2 mile away. Usually, people would just double park, instead.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> <P>Here's where it gets interesting...<BR>Seems like a car was double parked, blocking a police officer's personal vehicle. <BR>He called in a tag check. <BR>Tag check revealed that the car was stolen. Rented with a stolen credit card, several months before and never returned. <BR>A woman came out, and asked what was gong on.<BR>Officer: "Is this your car?"<BR>Woman: "Yeah. Sorry. I was in a hurry."<BR>They arrested her and searched her. She still had the stolen credit card in her purse. <P>DOH!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"><P>I think <I>she</I> had a bad day.  <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||RedHaze86SD4||11-29-2001||11:32 AM||||Was driving the car in my post "bribery??" home from work at 70 when the motor blew. It was 5:30pm just got off work and it was 30 something degrees (I was living up by Seattle) and there was enough traffic to keep you moving without using a motor. I had to coast across 2 lanes of traffic with Smoke pouring outta my car and after getting it out of the way I had to walk 2 and half miles to the nearest gas station to call my brother. Who wasn't home... So I had to wait at the gas station for 3 hours till I finanlly got someone to pick me up.... I think I turned three shades of blue walking without anyone even stopping to help... Then the damn fiero got towed the next morning before we got to it to take it home and I had to pay $450 to get it back from the Tow compnay... Was a very bad day for me.. ok ok so maybe 2 days :P<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/redhaze1_1.GIF"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||AusFiero||11-29-2001||04:20 PM||||My worse day would be when I worked 3 hours from home and was staying in Canberra.<BR>I came home from work for the weekend for my girlfriend of 3 years to dump me. Then I went to my place, which had been robbed. Cleaned out right down to the light fittings and curtains. After placing a police rport I went back to Canberra (where I was working) and got drunk (as you do). I then didn't want to leave my car with the last of my worldly belongings in it at the pub so I decided to drive it the 1km back to where I was staying (getting drunk wasn't planned hence the car being with me). Then I got done for driving under the influence.<BR>Arrggghhh.<BR><P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero3.gif">       <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
